Z||000000||Snowball||05-26-2001||05:17 PM||||where can I get the best information about wiring on a fiero? I bought a chiltons but it doesn't help much. I'm new to fiero's and don't have any local help or a lot of money. The car has a factory subwoofer radio and only one speaker is working the sub was disconnected and I would like some sounds. Anyone help would be great  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-26-2001||05:36 PM||||Best source, especially since you're in alaska, would be the <BR><A HREF="http://www.helminc.com" TARGET=_blank>Helm</A> shop book for your year. This is esentially the same book GM provides the dealers.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Snowball||05-26-2001||05:52 PM||||Thanks, do they have enough information to justify $90, I was a little let down with the chiltons information. I guess I'll just have to bite the bullet and spring for the book.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||Mark||05-26-2001||09:02 PM||||You may be able to find a used one on EBAY or in the mall section.  Save a few bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||05-26-2001||09:58 PM||||If you are planning on doing your own car work the Helm book is great.  It covers everything on the car---MUCH better than Chilton or Haynes.  The biggest drawback (other than price) is that the Helm book assumes you are using the special tools that the dealer has.  <P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
